    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231">

                <pb facs="0335" n="231" xml:id="pg231"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/2309: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Colombia
                        (Caffery)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-09-22T18:00:00-04:00">September 22,
                            1932—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. Your 74, September 21, 4 p.m. In informal discussion of certain of the
                    Neutrals it was suggested that they would ask their Governments to advise their
                    representatives at Geneva fully regarding the Chaco negotiations in order that
                    they would have the full background should the matter be brought up at the
                    League meeting. Department has no suggestion to make regarding endeavor to
                    persuade other Latin American delegates to instruct their delegates also but
                    leaves this matter to Olaya. The question has not been raised here. The only
                    point discussed was that the representatives at the League of the Neutral
                    Governments, members of the League, should be fully informed of the situation so
                    that they could handle it if it is brought up.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
